Reference quirks, two of them.

`vid` marks a paragraph that continues a verse begun earlier. The paragraph
after the table starts verse 3 itself (`\p` newline `\v 3`), after verse
2-7 ended inside the table, so it continues nothing; the usfm-js reference
gives it `vid="TIT 1:3"` anyway. Every other paragraph in the file that
starts with a verse has no `vid`.

`\fqa ... drink. \fv 8\fv* As the scripture ...`: the reference nests `\fv`
inside `\fqa` and keeps the text after `\fv*` in `\fqa`. The stylesheet does
not let `\fv` nest (no `NEST` in its `OccursUnder`), and Paratext writes
the same shape as siblings with the text after the closing marker as bare
note text (samples-from-wild/doo43-1, `\ft Instead of \fqa ...\fqa* , some
Greek copies read`). Same deviation as specExamples/footnote.

